ற்று","parts":[{"text":"மற்று","lemma":"மற்று","gloss":"then"}],"gloss":"then"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"பசி","parts":[{"text":"பசி","lemma":"பசி","gloss":"hunger"}],"gloss":"hunger"},{"surface":"தீர்ப்போரே","parts":[{"text":"தீர்ப்போர்","lemma":"தீர்ப்போர்","gloss":"those who satisfy"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"those who satisfy"}]}],"literal":"Very foolish indeed, oh Death without justice! / Because of lack of wisdom, you cooked and ate the seed! / Still you will see this becoming a true word: / Shining-sword warriors, and male elephants, and horses, / and blood, to be left behind on the fighting field of deep red water, / daily without ceasing, conquering and slaying, always your / fading hunger satisfying, guilt-removing power / like those of your lineage, wearing great ornaments made of gold, / Valavan called, who wears a bee-swarming garland, / such a person you took; if so, / who indeed then are those who will satisfy your hunger?","translation":"O Death, devoid of justice, you are utterly foolish! Out of sheer ignorance, you have cooked and eaten the very seed-grain! You will soon see the truth of this: he who daily, without fail, conquered and slew on the battlefield, leaving behind shining-sword warriors, elephants, horses, and blood flowing like a deep red river, thereby satisfying your fading hunger and removing your guilt with his power—that Valavan, wearing great golden ornaments like his ancestors and a garland swarmed by bees, you have taken away. If so, who is there now to satisfy your hunger?","modern":"நீதி இல்லாத கூற்றுவனே! நீ மிகவும் அறிவில்லாதவன். புத்தி இல்லாததால், விதை நெல்லையே சமைத்து உண்டுவிட்டாய். நான் சொல்வது உண்மை என்பதை நீ விரைவில் காண்பாய். ஒளிரும் வாளேந்திய வீரர்களும், யானைகளும், குதிரைகளும், குருதி பெருகும் போர்க்களத்திலேயே மடியுமாறு, நாள்தோறும் சளைக்காமல் வென்று கொன்று, உன்னுடைய வாடுகின்ற பசியைத் தீர்த்து உனது பழியைப் போக்கிய ஆற்றல் கொண்டவன் அவன். தன் முன்னோர்களைப் போலப் பொன்னால் செய்த பெரிய அணிகலன்களையும், வண்டுகள் மொய்க்கும் மாலையையும் அணிந்த வளவன் என்னும் பெயர் கொண்ட அத்தகையவனை நீ கொண்டு சென்றுவிட்டாய். இனிமேல் உன்னுடைய பசியைத் தீர்ப்பவர் யார் இருக்கிறார்கள்?","explanation":"The poet Āṭutuṟai Mācāttaṉār addresses Yama, the God of Death, on the demise of the Chola king Kiḷḷi Vaḷavaṉ. This poem belongs to the potuviyal tiṇai and the theme is kaiyaṟunilai, which expresses helpless grief over a death. The poet rebukes Death for committing a grave, foolish mistake, comparing the king to seed-grain (vittu). Just as a foolish farmer eats his seed-grain and starves in the future, Death has taken the king who used to feed him daily with the lives of enemies slain in battle. The key words are 'kūṟṟam' (Death), 'vittu' (seed), 'uṇṭaṉai' (you ate), and 'pasi' (hunger).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.24,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,1.6],[1.6,2.5],[2.5,2.5],[2.5,3.5],[3.5,4.0],[4.13,4.9],[4.9,5.4],[5.4,5.8],[5.8,6.3],[6.3,7.1],[7.1,7.6],[7.6,8.0],[8.0,8.4],[8.4,9.7],[9.7,10.22],[10.4,11.0],[11.0,11.4],[11.4,12.3],[12.3,12.5],[12.5,13.3],[13.3,13.7],[13.7,13.9],[13.9,14.7],[14.7,15.28],[15.28,15.5],[15.5,16.2],[16.32,16.93],[16.93,17.3],[17.3,18.0],[18.0,18.5],[19.24,19.84],[19.84,20.04],[20.04,20.64],[20.64,21.04],[21.04,21.84],[21.84,22.24],[22.24,22.24],[22.24,23.54],[23.54,23.64],[23.64,24.48],[24.48,24.56]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.2],[1.2,1.6],[1.6,1.9],[1.9,3.33],[3.33,3.8],[3.8,4.5],[4.5,4.9],[4.9,6.0],[6.0,6.6],[6.6,6.6],[6.6,7.4],[7.4,8.4],[8.4,8.5],[8.5,9.1],[9.1,9.6],[9.6,11.82],[11.82,12.1],[12.1,12.5],[12.5,13.0],[13.0,14.4],[14.4,14.8],[14.8,15.9],[15.9,16.3],[16.3,16.5],[16.5,17.9],[17.9,18.55],[18.55,18.8],[18.8,19.8],[19.98,20.9],[20.9,21.4],[21.4,21.9],[21.9,22.4],[23.12,23.82],[23.82,24.02],[24.02,24.72],[24.72,25.12],[25.12,26.12],[26.12,26.72],[26.72,27.02],[27.02,28.12],[28.12,28.22],[28.22,29.2],[29.2,29.26]]},"sync":[[["நனி","greatly"],["பேதையே","oh fool"]],[["பேதையே","oh fool"]],[["நயனில்","without justice"]],[["கூற்றம்","Death"]],[["விரகு","wisdom"],["இன்மையின்","because of lack"]],[["இன்மையின்","because of lack"]],[["வித்து","seed"],["அட்டு","having cooked"]],[["உண்டனை","you ate"]],[["இன்னும்","still"]],[["காண்குவை","you will see"]],[["நன்வாய்","truth"]],[["ஆகுதல்","becoming"]],[["ஒளிறு","shining"],["வாள்","sword"]],[["மறவரும்","and the warriors"]],[["களிறும்","and the male elephants"]],[["மாவும்","and the horses"]],[["குருதியும்","and the blood"]],[["குரூஉப்புனல்","deep red water"]],[["பொரு","fighting"],["களத்து","in the battlefield"]],[["ஒழிய","to perish"]],[["நாளும்","daily"]],[["ஆனான்","he who did not cease"]],[["கடந்து","having conquered"],["அட்டு","having slain"]],[["என்றும்","always"]],[["நின்","your"]],[["வாடு","fading"],["பசி","hunger"]],[["அருந்திய","that which satisfied"]],[["பழி","guilt"],["தீர்","removing"]],[["ஆற்றல்","power"]],[["நின்னோர்","those like you"]],[["அன்ன","like"]],[["பொன்","gold"],["இயல்","made of"]],[["பெரும்","great"],["பூண்","ornament"]],[["வளவன்","Valavan"]],[["என்னும்","called"]],[["வண்டு","bees"],["மூசு","swarming"]],[["கண்ணி","garland"]],[["இனையோன்","such a person"]],[["கொண்டனை","you took"]],[["ஆயின்","if so"]],[["இனியார்","who indeed now"]],[["மற்று","then"],["நின்","your"]],[["பசி","hunger"],["தீர்ப்போரே","those who satisfy"]],[["தீர்ப்போரே","those who satisfy"]]]}